# Local, per-session Claude Code state — including settings.local.json, which
# has accumulated over a thousand one-shot command allowances. The shared
# settings.json is tracked (see the negation below) so the repo's conventions
# reach a new session or a new person without being retyped.
.claude/*
!.claude/settings.json
site/

# Python bytecode from running pkgs/mneme's test suite in a workspace.
# jj auto-snapshots the WHOLE working copy, so these were committed by
# accident in #284 — there is no `git add` to scope and therefore no moment
# at which anyone was asked.  See CLAUDE.md's note on the auto-snapshot hazard.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
